<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT - M&amp;S raised at UBS.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - M&amp;S raised at UBS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Earnings estimates for Marks &amp; Spencer Plc were raised at UBS, market sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The stock was up 5-1/2p at 501-1/2 by 1351 GMT in a buoyant retail sector, with Next Plc up 12-1/2p at 563-1/2 and Boots Co Plc up 6p at 637.  </p>
<p>For the current year to March 1997, UBS raised its pre-tax profit forecast by 35 million stg to 1.16 billion stg and for the following year it raised by 50 million stg to 1.30 billion stg.</p>
<p>Sources said the upgrade reflected strong UK trading, with hopes that the autumn range would sell well because of recent cool weather.</p>
<p>A buoyant financial service performance and an improvement at Brooks Brothers in the U.S. were also behind the increase.</p>
<p>-- Jane Merriman, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
